For HW4, I used ChatGPT as a study assistant to understand graph problem-solving step by step. It helped me understand how to represent connected vertices using an adjacency list, why we use a queue (FIFO) in BFS to explore nodes level-by-level, and how the indegree + queue method produces a valid course ordering (and detects cycles by returning an empty list when not all courses can be processed).

My workflow was to first ask for pseudocode to understand the logic at a high level, then translate that pseudocode into Python code with line-by-line comments so I could clearly connect each line to what the algorithm is doing. I also used ChatGPT to debug mistakes like IndexError (list index out of range) by checking whether course labels stayed within 0..n-1 and validating inputs.

